# The release-coupled host bundle.
#
# Every file here is part of the contract between a release and the VPS it runs
# on: change one and a host that has not been updated can no longer be trusted
# to deploy the release that expects it. `infra/host-bundle/VERSION` is bumped
# whenever this inventory or any listed file changes; `MIN_VERSION` is bumped
# only when a release genuinely stops working on an older bundle.
#
# Files that are *not* release-coupled are deliberately absent: the Nginx site
# and TLS assets survive any release, and the backup unit files are installed
# by infra/backup/install-backups.sh on their own schedule.
#
# Format: <source-in-repository> <installed-destination> <mode>
infra/compose/compose.yaml /opt/ai-agent/docker-compose.yml 0644
infra/compose/compose.deploy.yaml /opt/ai-agent/docker-compose.deploy.yml 0644
infra/deploy/ai-agent-deploy /usr/local/sbin/ai-agent-deploy 0755
infra/deploy/ai-agent-deploy-dispatch /usr/local/sbin/ai-agent-deploy-dispatch 0755
infra/deploy/runtime-preflight.sh /usr/local/sbin/ai-agent-runtime-preflight 0755
infra/deploy/host-preflight.sh /usr/local/sbin/ai-agent-host-preflight 0755
infra/deploy/release-retention.sh /usr/local/sbin/ai-agent-release-retention 0755
infra/deploy/ai-agent-deploy.sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/ai-agent-deploy 0440
